  <ul><li><a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20151021065708/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Living+connections#David%20Barton">DBHB</a>'s great grandfather.</li><li>Born 25 February 1870, second youngest son of <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20151021065708/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Rev.+John+Barton+of+Cambridge+%281836-1908%29">Rev. John Barton of Cambridge (1836-1908)</a> and <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20151021065708/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Emily+Elliott+%281839-1924%29">Emily Elliott (1839-1924)</a>.</li><li>Full name 'Cecil Edward Barton'.</li><li>Contemporary of <span style="background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-color: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: 100% 50%; background-repeat: no-repeat no-repeat; cursor: pointer; padding-right: 10px;"><a class="wiki_link_ext" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20151021065708/http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahatma_Gandhi" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Gandhi (1869-1948)</a></span> and <span style="background-attachment: initial; background-clip: initial; background-color: initial; background-origin: initial; background-position: 100% 50%; background-repeat: no-repeat no-repeat; cursor: pointer; padding-right: 10px;"><a class="wiki_link_ext" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20151021065708/http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lenin" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lenin (1870-1924)</a></span>.</li><li>Missionary in India, spending some years in <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20151021065708/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Srinagar%2C+India">Srinagar, India</a>.</li><li>Married (on 21 October 1896 at <a class="wiki_link_ext" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20151021065708/http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murree" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Murree, now in Pakistan</a>), <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20151021065708/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Esther+Broadbent+%281873-1959%29">Esther Broadbent (1873-1959)</a>.</li><li>Amateur mountaineer whose <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20151021065708/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/%2ACecil+Barton+Mountaineering+Journals">expedition journals</a> we still have.</li><li>From 1904 to his death in 1909, was vicar of <a class="wiki_link_ext" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20151021065708/http://maps.google.co.uk/maps?q=Rousdon&amp;hl=en&amp;ll=50.7182,-3.001156&amp;spn=0.062494,0.154324&amp;sll=50.698415,-3.188095&amp;sspn=0.06252,0.154324&amp;oq=Rous&amp;hnear=Rousdon,+Devon,+United+Kingdom&amp;t=m&amp;z=13" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Rousdon, Devon</a>.</li><li>During this time, he authored of a <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20151021065708/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/%2ABarton+1910">book about his father</a>.</li><li>Father of <a class="wiki_link" href="/web/20151021065708/http://bartonhistory.wikispaces.com/Ronald+Barton+%281901-1986%29">Ronald Barton (1901-1986)</a>.</li><li>Died young 3 October 1909, aged 39.</li></ul><br/>
